Refuse a non-standard MIGraphX output instead of binding it to ORT's dense buffer

The compute function binds each "#output_N" parameter straight onto ORT's output tensor
with MIGraphX's shape for it. When that shape is a strided view (a partition that ends in
a Slice/Reshape; measured strides [32000, 2000, 40, 1] for lens [8, 16, 40, 40]), ORT reads
the strided bytes as dense and the write overruns the buffer, corrupting its neighbours:
wrong detections that drift between runs (BACKLOG CON225, RX 9070 XT, v1.31.0). Until the
provider copies such outputs through a contiguous buffer, fail loudly. Not in v1.31.1.

--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/migraphx/migraphx_execution_provider.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/migraphx/migraphx_execution_provider.cc
@@ -1577,6 +1577,11 @@
 
               // argument shape
               auto mgx_arg_shape = param_shapes[name];
+              // A strided view bound to ORT's dense buffer is read as dense and overruns it: refuse, never corrupt.
+              if (!mgx_arg_shape.standard()) {
+                ORT_THROW("MIGraphX output ", name, " is a non-standard (strided) view of ",
+                          mgx_arg_shape.bytes(), " bytes; ORT needs a dense tensor");
+              }
               m.add(name, migraphx::argument(mgx_arg_shape, output_data));
             }
           }
